Here is the input problem:
  Axiom 1 (implies_2): implies(true, X) = X.
  Axiom 2 (implies_1): implies(false, X) = true.
  Axiom 3 (leq_1): leq(zero, X) = true.
  Axiom 4 (leq_2): leq(suc(X), zero) = false.
  Axiom 5 (leq_3): leq(suc(X), suc(Y)) = leq(X, Y).
  Axiom 6 (eqNat_1): eqNat(zero, zero) = true.
  Axiom 7 (eqNat_2): eqNat(zero, suc(X)) = false.
  Axiom 8 (eqNat_3): eqNat(suc(X), zero) = false.
  Axiom 9 (eqNat_4): eqNat(suc(X), suc(Y)) = eqNat(X, Y).
  Axiom 10 (prop_leqAntisym_1): prop_leqAntisym(X, Y) = implies(leq(X, Y), eqNat(X, Y)).
  Axiom 11 (reflexivity): equals(X, X) = true.
  Axiom 12 (prop_leqAntisym): equals(prop_leqAntisym(X, Y), false) = false.
  Goal 1 (true_equals_false): true = false.

1. implies(true, X) -> X
2. implies(false, X) -> true
3. leq(zero, X) -> true
4. leq(suc(X), zero) -> false
5. leq(suc(X), suc(Y)) -> leq(X, Y)
6. eqNat(zero, zero) -> true
7. eqNat(zero, suc(X)) -> false
8. eqNat(suc(X), zero) -> false
9. eqNat(suc(X), suc(Y)) -> eqNat(X, Y)
10. implies(leq(X, Y), eqNat(X, Y)) -> prop_leqAntisym(X, Y)
11. equals(X, X) -> true
12. equals(prop_leqAntisym(X, Y), false) -> false
13. prop_leqAntisym(zero, zero) -> true
14. eqNat(zero, X) -> prop_leqAntisym(zero, X)
15. equals(true, false) -> false
16. prop_leqAntisym(suc(X), zero) -> true
17. prop_leqAntisym(zero, suc(X)) -> false
18. false -> true

The conjecture is true! Here is a proof.

Axiom 1 (implies_2): implies(true, X) = X.
Axiom 2 (leq_1): leq(zero, X) = true.
Axiom 3 (eqNat_2): eqNat(zero, suc(X)) = false.
Axiom 4 (prop_leqAntisym_1): prop_leqAntisym(X, Y) = implies(leq(X, Y), eqNat(X, Y)).

Goal 1 (prop_leqAntisym): prop_leqAntisym(X, Y) = false.
The goal is true when:
  X = zero
  Y = suc(X)

Proof:
  prop_leqAntisym(zero, suc(X))
= { by axiom 4 (prop_leqAntisym_1) }
  implies(leq(zero, suc(X)), eqNat(zero, suc(X)))
= { by axiom 3 (eqNat_2) }
  implies(leq(zero, suc(X)), false)
= { by axiom 2 (leq_1) }
  implies(true, false)
= { by axiom 1 (implies_2) }
  false

RESULT: Theorem (the conjecture is true).
